item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-489"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/contact-us/">Contact Us</a></li></ul></li></ul></div></nav><section class="categories"><header><div class="container"><h1>News</h1></div></header><main><div class="container"><ul><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/awards/">Awards</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/business/">Business</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/congress/">Congress</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/digital-media/">Digital Media</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/editorial/">Editorial</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/espanol/">Español</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/media-innovation/">Media Innovation</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/media-policy/">Media Policy</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/press-releases/">Press Corner</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/press-freedom/">Press Freedom</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/print-production/">Print</a></li><li class=""><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/category/women-in-news/">Women in News</a></li><li class="subscribe"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/newsletters/">Subscribe to Newsletters</a></li></ul></div></main></section><section class="single"><div class="container"><main><header><h1>World News Day: 21 Great Op-Eds on Why Journalism Matters</h1><h2><p>Ahead of World News Day on Monday, 28 September, 21 of the world&#8217;s leading journalists and media leaders explain why journalism matters now more than ever, writing on AI, press freedom, reporting in exile and the climate crisis.</p></h2></header><div class="image"> <img data-src="https://cdn.wan-ifra.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/27075258/WND-2026-OP-ED-QUOTES-1280-x-720-px.png" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==" class="lazyload" style="--smush-placeholder-width: 1280px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1280/720;"></div><div class="content-area"><div class="content"><p class="info"><strong>by WAN-IFRA Staff</strong> <a href="mailto:executivenews@wan-ifra.org" target="_blank">executivenews@wan-ifra.org</a> <strong>| September 25, 2026</strong></a></p><div class="text"><p dir="ltr">On Monday, September 28, more than 1,000 news organisations in 106 countries will mark World News Day by showing how their journalism makes a difference. Ahead of the day, the campaign has published a strong collection of op-eds from veteran journalists, editors and media leaders, including Tina Brown, Lionel Barber and AFP&#8217;s Phil Chetwynd. They cover the threat of AI and misinformation, press freedom under pressure, reporting from exile and war zones, the climate crisis, and why local news still counts.</p><p dir="ltr">All of the op-eds are free to republish with appropriate credit. Read the full collection at <a href="https://worldnewsday.org/stories/">worldnewsday.org/stories</a>, or start with the list below.</p><ul dir="ltr"><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/the-integrity-dividend-the-value-of-knowing/">The Integrity Dividend: The Value of Knowing</a></strong> by David Walmsley (World Editors Forum / Globe and Mail), Mariya Gabriel (UNESCO) and Liz Corbin (European Broadcasting Union)</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/journalism-our-chaotic-worlds-future/">Journalism &amp; Our Chaotic World&#8217;s Future</a></strong> by Branko Brkic (Project Kontinuum) and Tina Brown (Truth Tellers)</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/footballs-enduring-controversies-show-why-journalism-matters/">Football&#8217;s enduring controversies show why journalism matters</a></strong> by Stig Ørskov, CEO of WAN-IFRA</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/media-faces-violence-persecution-and-the-existential-threat-posed-by-ai-and-yet-we-are-still-here/">Media faces violence, persecution and the existential threat posed by AI – and yet we are still here</a></strong> by Marcelo Rech, Executive President of the Brazilian Newspaper Association (ANJ)</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/democracy-needs-journalism-in-every-language/">Democracy Needs Journalism in Every Language</a></strong> by Anna Mae Lamentillo, Founder of Paraluman News, The Philippines</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/indias-students-found-their-voice-this-summer-while-journalists-are-losing-theirs/">India&#8217;s students found their voice this summer while journalists are losing theirs</a></strong> by Ritu Kapur</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/dystopia-inc-would-you-like-your-news-with-or-without-hallucinations/">Dystopia, Inc: Would you like your news with or without hallucinations?</a></strong> by Phil Chetwynd, Global News Director at AFP</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/truth-in-an-ai-world/">Truth in an AI World</a></strong> by Michael Miller, Executive Chairman of News Corp Australasia <em>(Embargoed: not for publication before September 28, 2026)</em></li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/a-lesson-from-ukraine-newsroom-resilience-makes-press-freedom-real/">A lesson from Ukraine: Newsroom resilience makes press freedom real</a></strong> by Oksana Brovko, CEO of the Association of Independent Regional Press Publishers of Ukraine</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/free-press-needs-alliances-against-censorship-and-fragmentation/">Free press needs alliances against censorship and fragmentation</a></strong> by Natalia Antelava</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/thank-goodness-for-the-storytellers-the-ones-who-probe-question-irritate-the-powerful/">Thank goodness for the storytellers – the ones who probe, question, irritate the powerful</a></strong> by Meera Selva, CEO of Informed</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/america-was-the-arsenal-of-democracy-now-its-disarming-the-press/">America Was the Arsenal of Democracy; Now It&#8217;s Disarming the Press</a></strong> by Lionel Barber</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/when-information-is-everywhere-and-the-reasons-to-give-up-are-so-many-journalism-matters-even-more/">When information is everywhere, and the reasons to give up are so many… journalism matters even more</a></strong> by Garry Pierre-Pierre</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/remembering-9-11-as-a-local-news-story/">Remembering 9-11 as a local news story</a></strong> by Charles M. Sennott</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/independent-news-media-need-more-than-short-term-funding/">Independent News Media Need More Than Short-Term Funding</a></strong> by Caroline Vuillemin, Director General of Fondation Hirondelle</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/nicaragua-reinventing-journalism-in-exile/">Nicaragua: Reinventing Journalism in Exile</a></strong> by Carlos Fernando Chamorro, Director of Confidencial and 2024 Golden Pen of Freedom Laureate</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/the-things-i-learned-from-my-daughters-a-central-bank-investigation-and-a-box-of-watermelon-gum/">The things I learned from my daughters, a central bank investigation, and a box of watermelon gum</a></strong> by Alia Ibrahim, Co-founder and CEO of Daraj.com</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/the-role-of-the-news-media-in-fighting-the-climate-crisis/">The role of the news media in fighting the climate crisis</a></strong> by Kyle Pope</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/journalism-is-civic-infrastructure-we-need-to-support-it/">Journalism is Civic Infrastructure. We need to support it.</a></strong> by Alberto Ibargüen</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/we-must-make-truth-matter-again/">We must make truth matter again</a></strong> by Fernando Belzunce, Editorial General Director of Vocento</li><li><strong><a href="https://worldnewsday.org/2026-world-news-day-time-to-fight/">2026 World News Day: Time to fight</a></strong> by Branko Brkic</li></ul><div class="addtoany_share_save_container addtoany_content addtoany_content_bottom"><div class="a2a_kit a2a_kit_size_32 addtoany_list" data-a2a-url="https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/world-news-day-21-great-op-eds-on-why-journalism-matters/" data-a2a-title="World News Day: 21 Great Op-Eds on Why Journalism Matters"><a class="a2a_button_facebook" href="https://www.addtoany.com/add_to/facebook?linkurl=https%3A%2F%2Fwan-ifra.org%2F2026%2F09%2Fworld-news-day-21-great-op-eds-on-why-journalism-matters%2F&amp;linkname=World%20News%20Day%3A%2021%20Great%20Op-Eds%20on%20Why%20Journalism%20Matters" title="Facebook" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"></a><a class="a2a_button_twitter" href="https://www.addtoany.com/add_to/twitter?linkurl=https%3A%2F%2Fwan-ifra.org%2F2026%2F09%2Fworld-news-day-21-great-op-eds-on-why-journalism-matters%2F&amp;linkname=World%20News%20Day%3A%2021%20Great%20Op-Eds%20on%20Why%20Journalism%20Matters" title="Twitter" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"></a><a class="a2a_button_linkedin" href="https://www.addtoany.com/add_to/linkedin?linkurl=https%3A%2F%2Fwan-ifra.org%2F2026%2F09%2Fworld-news-day-21-great-op-eds-on-why-journalism-matters%2F&amp;linkname=World%20News%20Day%3A%2021%20Great%20Op-Eds%20on%20Why%20Journalism%20Matters" title="LinkedIn" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"></a><a class="a2a_dd addtoany_share_save addtoany_share" href="https://www.addtoany.com/share"></a></div></div></div><div class="profile"><div class="avatar" style="background-image: url('https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/faf39a734271d7990e9fa9644c11afc5a8ab012277312bbe7ef6f1cfabf4f33c?s=100&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g');"></div><div class="text-area"><p><strong>WAN-IFRA Staff</strong></p><p><a href="mailto:executivenews@wan-ifra.org" target="_blank">executivenews@wan-ifra.org</a></p></div></div></div></div></main><aside><section> <img data-src="https://cdn.wan-ifra.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/24133822/Wan-Ifra-logotype-World-Editors-Forum_white-1.png" alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==" class="lazyload" style="--smush-placeholder-width: 9305px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 9305/2000;" /><p>The World Editors Forum is the leading global community of editors and is an integral part of WAN-IFRA. We stand up for a free press, quality journalism and newsroom transformation, and have been doing so for over 25 years. We work with editors to shape their newsrooms for the future. We do so by identifying innovation and trends, tools and best practices. We share this intelligence through our blog, newsletter, meetings, networking events, conferences, and research.</p></section><section class="related"><h1 class="title">Related Posts</h1> <a href="https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/america-the-arsenal-of-democracy-is-now-disarming-the-press/" class="post"><div class="image lazyload" style="background-image:inherit;" data-bg-image="url(&#039;https://cdn.wan-ifra.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/28145245/WND-Lionel-Barber.jpg&#039;)"></div><h1>America, the &#8216;arsenal of democracy,&#8217; is now disarming the press</h1> </a> <a href="https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/nicaragua-reinventing-journalism-in-exile/" class="post"><div class="image lazyload" style="background-image:inherit;" data-bg-image="url(&#039;https://cdn.wan-ifra.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/28142016/WND-Carlos-Chamorro.jpg&#039;)"></div><h1>Nicaragua: Reinventing Journalism in Exile</h1> </a> <a href="https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/the-integrity-dividend-the-value-of-knowing/" class="post"><div class="image lazyload" style="background-image:inherit;" data-bg-image="url(&#039;https://cdn.wan-ifra.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/24073903/WND_OP-ED_DAVID-WALMSLEY_BLUE.jpg&#039;)"></div><h1>The Integrity Dividend: The Value of Knowing</h1> </a></section></aside></div></section><footer id="main"><div class="container"><p>&copy; <script>document.write(new Date().getFullYear());</script> WAN-IFRA</p><p>World Association of News Publishers</p><ul id="menu-footer-menu" class="menu"><li id="menu-item-11906" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-home menu-item-11906"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/">Landing page</a></li><li id="menu-item-39312" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-39312"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/about-us/">About Us</a></li><li id="menu-item-69516" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-69516"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/newsletters/">Newsletters</a></li><li id="menu-item-8148" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-8148"><a href="https://wan-ifra.org/imprint/">Imprint</a></li><li id="menu-item-135" class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-135"><a rel="privacy-policy" href="https://wan-ifra.org/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a></li></ul></div></footer><div id="output"></div> <script type="speculationrules">{"prefetch":[{"source":"document","where":{"and":[{"href_matches":"/*"},{"not":{"href_matches":["/wp-*.php","/wp-admin/*","/wp-content/uploads/*","/wp-content/*","/wp-content/plugins/*","/wp-content/themes/wan-ifra/*","/*\\?(.+)"]}},{"not":{"selector_matches":"a[rel~=\"nofollow\"]"}},{"not":{"selector_matches":".no-prefetch, .no-prefetch a"}}]},"eagerness":"conservative"}]}</script> <script type="text/javascript" src="//s3.amazonaws.com/downloads.mailchimp.com/js/mc-validate.js"></script><script type="text/javascript">(function($) {window.fnames = new Array(); window.ftypes = new Array();fnames[0]='EMAIL';ftypes[0]='email';fnames[1]='FNAME';ftypes[1]='text';fnames[2]='LNAME';ftypes[2]='text';fnames[5]='CONTACTID';ftypes[5]='text';fnames[4]='GENDER';ftypes[4]='tex